# Local auto-commit after each change

When you finish a coherent code/docs change in this repo, **create a local git commit** before ending the turn (unless the user said not to commit that change).

## Rules

- Commit only to the local repo; **do not push** unless the user explicitly asks
- Follow the existing git safety protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no `--no-verify`, no amend unless amend rules apply)
- One commit per logical change when practical; include related files together
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, etc.)
- Testing remains disabled per `no-testing.mdc` — commits are for feature/docs work only
